'''United States gubernatorial elections''' were held in 12 states (including a [[2012 Wisconsin gubernatorial recall election|recall election]] in [[Wisconsin]] on June 5) and two territories. Of the eight [[Democratic Party (United States)|Democratic]] and four [[Republican Party (United States)|Republican]] seats contested, only that of [[2012 North Carolina gubernatorial election|North Carolina]] changed party hands, giving the Republicans a net gain of one governorship. These elections (except for [[2012 Wisconsin gubernatorial recall election|Wisconsin]]) coincided with the [[2012 United States presidential election|presidential election]] on November 6, 2012. As of 2024, this marked the last time in which a Democrat won the governorship in Missouri, and the last time in which a Republican won the governorship in North Carolina.

